From b42714ba63fe83d7357a624b4f86a2188ea989cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 06:54:26 +0000
Subject: Offer a download for audio elements

Long pressing an <audio> element produced a menu with nothing on it. The cause
was not the menu but the plumbing: ContextMenuParams has always been handed the
media type, and ContextMenuDataMediaType.AUDIO has always arrived, but only
IMAGE and VIDEO were ever read out of it, so audio fell through to no group at
all.

Exposing isAudio() and adding a group for it is the whole change. The download
itself reuses the video path exactly, through ContextMenuItemDelegate
startDownload and the native delegate, so it obeys the same policy check, the
same downloadable scheme check, the same kMediaCanSave gate, and Bare's
external download manager handoff. No second downloader.

Opening a menu on an audio element also meant producing a ContextMenuParams
shape upstream has never seen, and two places were not ready for it.
getContextMenuTypeForHistogram walked its chain of media kinds, found none of
them, and hit an assertion meant for anchors, which took the whole browser down
the moment the menu appeared. It now has an audio branch. The suffix it returns
is not in histogram_suffixes_list.xml, which is an upstream file not worth
touching for a downstream-only menu, so those samples land unmapped, which is
the right trade. getTitle had the same gap and returned an empty header; it now
names the file like it does for image and video.

Two deliberate choices for rebase safety. SAVE_AUDIO is appended to the end of
the Item enum rather than grouped next to SAVE_VIDEO, because the menu id and
string arrays are indexed by those values and inserting in the middle would
renumber everything after it. And no UMA action is recorded, since the
histogram enum is upstream and adding a value would mean editing enums.xml for
a downstream-only item.

ChromeContextMenuPopulator is a large file that churns upstream, so the
additions there are two contiguous blocks rather than being spread through it.
